 folder←NormalizeFolder folder
⍝ Returns `folder` in the one and only form APLGit2 uses internally: slashes rather than
⍝ backslashes, and NO trailing separator.\\
⍝ Rationale: almost every consumer builds a path with `folder,'/',whatever`, so a trailing
⍝ separator would result in a double one. An empty argument is returned unchanged, and so are
⍝ "/" and "C:/" - dropping the separator would change their meaning.
 :If 0<≢folder
     folder←F.EnforceSlash folder
     :If 2<≢folder
     :AndIf '/'=¯1↑folder
     :AndIf ':'≠⊃¯1↑¯1↓folder
         folder←¯1↓folder
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
